		Design decisions worth knowing
		It does not write a Call_Log row. callCenter already logs agent-placed calls, and getCallbackStatus creates one for any call it can't match. Logging here too would race both and duplicate rows for the same call.
		
		Ticket links open in a new tab. The agent dashboard can't be framed — that's the whole reason we're on a public page — so there's nowhere else inside Ozonetel's panel for them to go.
		
		The $CallerID$ guard is carried over. If the token arrives unsubstituted, the panel says so plainly instead of running a lookup that can only match nothing. Given Ozonetel proved it doesn't substitute tokens on URL to Push, that's a live possibility here.
		
		⚠️ The phone parameter name is still unconfirmed for ScreenPop. The widget accepts 18 spellings, so if Ozonetel sends $ANI$ or $From$ you only change the URL — but the browser console lists whatever actually arrives, so one test call settles it.
		
		
		c#1-104
		do i need to create page variable
		Yes — phone is required. Without it nothing reaches the widget.
		
		Why
		The widget runs in an iframe whose URL is Zoho's, not your page's. It can't read the parent page's query string — that's cross-origin. ZOHO.CREATOR.UTIL.getQueryParams() is the only channel, and it returns only parameters that are declared as Page Variables and mapped to the widget element.
		
		This is the exact thing that blocked the Dashboard_2 screen-pop earlier — it saw only serviceOrigin until you declared phone.
		
		The widget does have hash and query-string fallbacks, but those only help when the page is opened directly for testing. Inside the real page they see the iframe's own URL, which is empty.
		
		What to create on the InboundCall page
		Variable	Type	Needed?
		phone	Single Line	🔴 Required
		ucid	Single Line	Optional — shows the call ID in the header
		type	Single Line	Optional — shows "Inbound" vs "Outbound"
		Only phone drives the lookup. Drop ucid and type from the ScreenPop URL if you'd rather not declare them — the pop works fine on the number alone.
		
