		That changes everything — and opens a much better option. Let me look at the nesting:
		
		
		Zoho Creator page (Dashboard_2)   ← you control this
		  └─ iframe → agent.cloudagent.ozonetel.com
			   └─ iframe → "Pop CRM" → a Zoho page   ← DENY blocks this
		Ozonetel is running inside your page. So instead of asking Ozonetel to render Zoho inside itself, the pop can live on the parent page — where callCenter already is, with its screen-pop UI already built. It just needs a trigger other than the URL.
		
		Let me check whether CloudAgent tells the parent anything.
		
		
		That iframe snippet explains the whole problem — and points at a better fix than a new tab.
		
		Why the Pop CRM panel fails
		
		Zoho page (Dashboard_2)
		  └─ iframe → agent.cloudagent.ozonetel.com     ← your snippet
			   └─ iframe → Pop CRM → a Zoho page        ← "refused to connect"
		Ozonetel is asking to render Zoho inside a frame that is itself already inside Zoho. Zoho's X-Frame-Options: DENY blocks that, and no page you point at will change it.
		
		The better route
		Ozonetel is running inside your page, and callCenter — which already has the screen-pop UI, ticket matching and Call_Log write — is on that same page. It doesn't need Ozonetel to render anything. It just needs to know a call arrived.
		
		A child iframe can't be read across origins, but it can postMessage to its parent, and many CTI toolbars announce call events that way. Whether CloudAgent does isn't documented anywhere we have — so I've added a listener that answers it.
		
		What I added to callCenter
		A diagnostic: every postMessage this page receives is logged with its origin and payload. One inbound call and the console says definitively whether CloudAgent posts anything, and in what shape.
		
		A trigger: if a message carries something that looks like a phone number, it opens the existing pop. No new UI — it reuses renderIncomingCallPop() exactly as the URL route does.
		
		Guarded deliberately:
		
		Guard	Why
		Origin must be an ozonetel.com host	Won't react to unrelated frames
		10–15 digits required	Ignores IDs, timestamps, junk
		Same number within 30s ignored	The toolbar re-announcing one call isn't two calls
		A pop that shouldn't have opened is worse than none, because it writes a Call_Log row.
		
		Upload and test
		callCenter/dist/callCenter.zip → then make one inbound call with the console open.
		
		Console shows	Meaning
		postMessage from https://agent.cloudagent.ozonetel.com | {...}	✅ CloudAgent talks to the parent — send me the payload and I'll map it exactly
		Pop opens by itself	✅ Already working
		Nothing at all	CloudAgent doesn't post to its parent. This route is closed, and asking Ozonetel for new-tab ScreenPop is the answer
		Either outcome is a real answer, and it costs one call to get. boot() is unchanged when called without an override, so the existing URL route and everything else on the page behave exactly as before.
		
		
		
