		Both files patched. The loop had two latent faults, not one: toList("") isn't valid Deluge, and phoneChar >= "0" is the same string-comparison construct that threw "Comparison of non numeric expression is not supported" earlier in this project. The replacement uses a while over subText() and a digitChars.contains() test — no string ordering, no empty delimiter.
		
		
		digitsOnly = "";
		digitChars = "0123456789";
		charIndex = 0;
		phoneLength = rawPhone.length();
		while(charIndex < phoneLength)
		{
			phoneChar = rawPhone.subText(charIndex,charIndex + 1);
			if(digitChars.contains(phoneChar))
			{
				digitsOnly = digitsOnly + phoneChar;
			}
			charIndex = charIndex + 1;
