		Two things you should know before sending it, because they're the likeliest sources of a client question:
		
		Cash Collected is derived, not entered. It equals Remaining_Fee, but only when Payment_Method_Final is "Cash" and Payment_received is "Yes". Booking Fee is deliberately excluded, as are UPI/Card/Net Banking. That's a commercial decision sitting in code, so it's listed under Points to verify.
		TDS is calculated on the batch, not per case. Per-case figures are proportional shares with largest-remainder paise allocation, so they sum exactly to what Zoho Books is told. A client checking one case's TDS against Net Fee × rate will find a paise difference and it will look like a bug.
		One gap worth flagging separately: a TOW case whose Vehicle_Issue contains neither FBT nor MT resolves to no slab field, so no fee is calculated at all and the case can't be approved. That's in the doc, but it's an operational trap rather than a field definition.
		
		
