		Fixed in all three vendor-side apps and packed. There were two defects, and the second one is the serious one.
		
		Defect 1 — the dropdown never showed the stored value. The five options were hardcoded with <option value="Cash" selected>. So a ticket that paymentWebhook.deluge had already marked "Payment Gateway" still displayed Cash when the screen was reopened. It now pre-selects whatever the ticket holds, falling back to Cash only if the stored value isn't one of the five.
		
		Defect 2 — clicking "Payment Received" overwrote a real gateway payment. The button is enabled once Payment_received === "Yes", and the payload wrote Payment_Method_Final unconditionally from that defaulted dropdown. So one click on a gateway-settled ticket silently rewrote "Payment Gateway" → "Cash". The payload now omits that field when the gateway already settled the payment; everything else is written exactly as before, so a normal cash/UPI/card close is unchanged.
		
		That second one is a money bug, not a display bug. cashCollectedForTicket() deducts the Remaining Fee from the vendor's payout whenever this field reads "Cash" — so a mislabelled gateway payment underpays the vendor by money the customer never handed them.
		
