		Three places I deviated from the sheets, and why
		The CONTINUE gate is not implemented. The sheets say "SEND 1, ON CLICK OF [cta] CONTINUE, SEND 2 AND THEN SEND 3". Knowing the customer tapped CONTINUE needs WhatsPortal posting an inbound event back to us, and nothing here receives one. So 1, 2 and 3 go out in sequence and 3 fires regardless. The customer sees all three messages; what's lost is the pause. initiate_conversation is the only MARKETING template and can be refused by marketing opt-out, so it's best-effort — it can never stop the fee or location request going out.
		
		SEND 9 goes immediately, not after 5 minutes. A widget can't hold a 5-minute timer; the app gets closed and the message never arrives. Delivered-now beats delivered-never. Honouring the gap needs a scheduled Deluge function sweeping a due-time field — new Zoho infrastructure, and a separate piece of work whenever you want it.
		
		SEND 12 is not auto-sent on COMPLETE/DROPPED. The sheets pair it with 11 when a balance is owed, but that screen already has its own "Send Payment Link" button — auto-sending would deliver two identical links, and you asked earlier for no automatic link sends. The agent-side BALANCE FEE REQUEST does send both, exactly as specced.
		
		What to watch on the first live run
		The one existing behaviour I changed is SEND 12's gate: it used to fire on every Balance Fee Request click, so a ₹0 ticket sent a payment link for nothing. It now sends 11 alone when the balance is zero.
		
		Everything else is additive. Every new send is best-effort — failures log or toast but never block a save, a completion or a status change. SEND 5/6/7 fire only on a real status transition, so re-saving a step sends nothing.
		
		Still unresolved from earlier: whether confirm_customer_location_details_copy or confirm_customer_location_details is the live name. One GET /templates?status=APPROVED&limit=50 settles it, and I've left the code alone until it does.
		
		
