		Both fixed in all three field apps — upload vendorTicket, technicianTicket and driverTicket.
		
		1. Vehicle name missing on Android
		It's a layout bug, not a data one — both devices receive the same name, and I verified the resolver: vehicleDisplayFor() reads VEHICLE_NAMES[id] from a 1000-record fetch awaited before first render, with a Custom API fallback if the report read is denied. Nothing device-specific there.
		
		The card is a two-column grid sized 1fr 1fr. A 1fr track keeps min-width: auto, so it refuses to shrink below its content's min-content width. Long unbroken values — "OTHER TWO WHEELER", "PUNCTURE-TUBELESS TYRE" — push the column wider than the card and overflow instead of wrapping. iOS Safari and Android Chrome differ in viewport width and font metrics, which is exactly why it fits on iPhone and clips on Android.
		
		
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr)   /* track may now shrink */
		.info-grid .v { min-width:0; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word }
		Purely additive — it permits shrinking and wrapping that were previously refused, so anything that already fits renders identically. iOS is unchanged.
		
		2. Phone tap-to-dial on Android
		The link was already there and the URI was already correct — formatIndianPhone() produces +917210036790, no spaces. The frame was the problem. The widget runs in a cross-origin iframe, and Android Chrome blocks an iframe navigating itself to an external scheme. iOS intercepts tel: at the OS level regardless, which is precisely why it worked on iPhone.
		
		Added target="_top" rel="noopener". Top-level navigation is permitted with user activation, and the OS takes over the tel: scheme before any page load begins, so the widget is never actually unloaded.
		
		Worth testing on a real Android handset
		Both fixes are browser-behaviour fixes, so an emulator or desktop responsive mode won't prove them. On a real Android phone, open a ticket and check: the vehicle name wraps onto two lines instead of being cut off, and tapping the number opens the dialler with it pre-filled.
		
