		Same URL, same API, same registration. The only difference is what's in the request body. Flow is sending an empty one.
		
		The likely mistake
		Zoho Flow's Send Webhook screen usually has two places to put values:
		
		Query Parameters — appended to the URL after ?
		Body / Payload — the actual request body
		If the four values went into Query Parameters, that's exactly this symptom. I tested it: a POST-registered Creator API ignores query parameters entirely and reads only the body. My probe with the values in the URL returned all four as (null) — an exact match for what you're seeing.
		
		So: move them to the Body section, and set the content type there to JSON.
		
		
		callerID  →  payload.callerID
		ucid      →  payload.ucid
		type      →  payload.type
		agentID   →  payload.agentID
		Take each value from Flow's variable picker rather than typing it, and keep the key spelling exactly as above — callerID with a capital I and D.
		
