		{
		  "data": <Webhook → Payload>
		}
		That sends one key called data containing the whole payload object. But recordRingingCall has four separate parameters — callerID, ucid, type, agentID — and no parameter called data. So Creator finds none of them and hands all four to the function as null. Exactly what you're seeing.
		
		You've copied the shape from the getCallbackStatus flow, which is reasonable — but that API does have a data parameter and parses the blob itself. This one takes discrete fields instead.
		
