		}
		For each <chip>: click inside the quotes, then in the Insert variable panel on the right click Webhook → Incoming Webhook to expand it, then Payload, then pick callerID, ucid, type, agentID individually. The trigger has already captured a real call, so Flow knows all fourteen field names and will list them.
		
		Keep the double quotes around each chip. All four values are strings, and callerID in particular arrives as " 917210036790" with a leading space — unquoted, that isn't valid JSON at all and the whole body would be rejected.
		
