		Anything that messages the customer — location links, payment links — should go out when an agent clicks a button, not automatically when a ticket reaches a stage. On 2026-09-25 the user asked for the automatic breakdown-location send to be removed ("don't share automatically location link in this"), leaving only the manual button.
		
		**Why:** agents want control over what the customer receives and when. An automatic send also duplicates the manual button that already exists on the same screen, so the customer gets the same message twice.
		
		**How to apply:** when a spec says a message fires on reaching a status or completing a step, check whether a manual button for that same message already exists. If it does, wire the button and flag the automatic path rather than building both. Applied this way when the LOGIC-REPAIR/LOGIC-TOW sheets paired SEND 11 with SEND 12 on COMPLETE/DROPPED — SEND 11 was wired, SEND 12 left to its existing button. Status-milestone messages (SEND 5/6/7) are the exception: they have no button and no other trigger, so they do fire automatically.
		
