		Good. A few things that'll make debugging faster if something misbehaves:
		
		Keep the browser console open. Every new path logs its own line with a [Get-Rescue] or [GR-CallCenter] prefix, including what it tried to send — so a failure usually names itself rather than needing a guess.
		
		What a WhatsApp failure looks like: nothing arrives and the app shows no error. The console line for that send tells you the template name and parameters; a 422 means a parameter count mismatch, a 404 means the template name is wrong.
		
		What a screen-pop failure looks like: no RINGING row in Call_Log_Report. If the row appears but no pop, that's the widget or the poll; if no row, that's still the Flow body.
		
		Two rows for one call means getCallbackStatus wasn't re-pasted — the UCID match fails and it creates a second row instead of completing the first.
		
