		No — those nine are the vendor payout rate card only. There are two completely separate pricing systems in this app, and they don't share a single field:
		
		What the customer pays	What the vendor is paid
		Source	Rate_Master_Report	Vendors_Report (your nine fields)
		Keyed on	Vehicle Type + Vehicle Segment + Issue	The assigned vendor
		Produces	Suggested_Rate, Rate_Breakup → Total_Service_Fee	KM Fee → Gross → Net → Final Payable
		Where	Quote step	Vendor Accounting
		So a customer being charged ₹2,400 and a vendor being paid ₹1,100 on the same job are two independent calculations. Changing a KM_Rate on a vendor never moves a customer quote, and editing Rate_Master never changes a payout.
		
		And even within the payout, those nine aren't the whole picture — they're the rates. The amounts come from the ticket:
		
		Vendor_Distance / Vendor_Round_Trip_Distance — the actual KM the rate is applied to
		Extras — added to Gross to reach Net
		Remaining_Fee + Payment_Method_Final + Payment_received — the Cash Collected deduction
		Service_Type, Vehicle_Issue, Vehicle — which of the five KM slabs applies
		A useful way to hold it: Vendors_Report supplies the rates, Create_Case supplies the quantities. Neither calculates anything alone.
		
		One thing worth flagging while we're here — Rate_Master_Report is marked in the code as a best-guess report name, never confirmed live (widget.html:743). If Suggested Rate ever comes back blank on the Quote step, that name is the first thing to check.
		
		
