		Payment and Invoicing Fields is up — three flows, every field, and three worked examples.
		
		Every number in the examples came from running the live formulas, not from hand arithmetic.
		
		One thing surfaced while writing example 2 that I want to put in front of you, because it isn't a documentation point — it's an operational one.
		
		A vendor who collects more cash than their payout cannot be paid
		Take the example 1 job and change a single field, Payment_Method_Final, from Payment Gateway to Cash:
		
		Vendor Net Fee	₹1,700.00
		Cash Collected	₹2,000.00
		Final Payable	−₹317.00
		The vendor is holding ₹300 that belongs to the company. recordVendorPayment.deluge's pre-flight guard rejects a negative Final Payable and writes nothing to Zoho Books — so that batch can't be settled at all.
		
		The guard is right to exist: it was added after a bug left orphaned bills and credits in Books with no payment against them. But it has no path for money flowing the other way, and this isn't an edge case — it's the normal shape of a margin business. Customer charged ₹2,500, vendor paid ₹1,700, customer pays the balance in cash. Any job where the cash the vendor collects exceeds their payout hits it.
		
		Neither the Vendor Accounting PDF nor the invoicing PDF covers vendor-owes-company. The usual answer is a recoverable balance carried to that vendor's next payment run, but that's a commercial decision, not a technical one — so I've documented it rather than picking one.
		
		Worth raising with the client before the first live payment run, since it'll show up the moment a cash-settled job goes through.
		
		
